{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.WignerCoefficientDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.WignerCoefficientDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.HeckeMassElement","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WignerCoefficient.ConditionalAudit.wigner_coefficient_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WignerCoefficient.ConditionalAudit.wigner_coefficient_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-coefficient-derivation.lean#L77-L86","doc":"**Conditional on `conj:q-integer-mass-formula`.** For a\nnon-negative electron-mass scale, every liquid-drop coefficient is\na non-negative multiple of `m_e` (so all are non-negative). Derived\nfrom the class field, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WignerCoefficient.ConditionalAudit.QIntegerMassFormula.coeffs_are_q_rational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WignerCoefficient.ConditionalAudit.QIntegerMassFormula.coeffs_are_q_rational","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-coefficient-derivation.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Each liquid-drop coefficient is `m_e` scaled by a non-negative\nsubstrate-derived `q`-rational ratio (existence of the ratio\nfamily is the conjectural input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WignerCoefficient.ConditionalAudit.QIntegerMassFormula.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WignerCoefficient.ConditionalAudit.QIntegerMassFormula.mk","kind":"ctor","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-coefficient-derivation.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WignerCoefficient.ConditionalAudit.QIntegerMassFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WignerCoefficient.ConditionalAudit.QIntegerMassFormula","kind":"class","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-coefficient-derivation.lean#L57-L75","doc":"**§3b-cond hypothesis class** for `conj:q-integer-mass-formula`.\n\nThe empirical Bethe–Weizsäcker liquid-drop coefficients\n(`λ_V, λ_S, λ_C, a_asym, …`) are each a product of quantum integers\n`[n]_q = (q^n − q^{-n})/(q − q^{-1})` evaluated at the substrate\nparameter `q₀`, times the electron mass `m_e` — i.e. each empirical\ncoefficient equals a substrate-derived algebraic `q`-rational\nmultiple of `m_e`, not a free fit parameter.\n\nConcrete content (shape of the claim): for every empirical\ncoefficient `c` (indexed by `ℕ`) there is a non-negative\n`q`-rational ratio `r` with `c = r · m_e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.wigner_coefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.wigner_coefficient","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-coefficient-derivation.lean#L44-L48","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:wigner-coefficient-derivation","label":"prop:wigner-coefficient-derivation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-coefficient-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.wigner_coefficient_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.wigner_coefficient_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-coefficient-derivation.lean#L31-L42","doc":"**External axiom (§3b-cond pattern): wigner_coefficient.**\n\nAuto-extracted from the single-sorry theorem body in this file.\nEncodes the categorical content pending Mathlib infrastructure\nor a structure-tightening refactor.\n\nSee the theorem docstring below for the cited reference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.wignerCoefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.wignerCoefficient","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-coefficient-derivation.lean#L26-L28","doc":"The Wigner coefficient at level k is [k]_q! · m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qFactorial","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-coefficient-derivation.lean#L22-L24","doc":"The quantum factorial [n]_q! = Π_{k=1}^n [k]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qInt","kind":"def","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-coefficient-derivation.lean#L15-L20","doc":"Quantum n-integer `[n]_q = (q^n − q^{-n}) / (q − q^{-1})`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}